speechtext:
Resolved, that a sum not exceeding $965,328,156.84 being the aggregate of-
(a)	four twelfths of the total of all the items set forth in the main estimates for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1968, laid before the House of Commons at the present session of parliament and not otherwise provided for, except public service commission item 5 and loans, investments and advances item L40, for which no proportion is granted hereby, $889,450,033.33;
(b)	four twelfths of the total amount of Public Works item 65 (Schedule A) of the said main estimates, $4,883,333.33;
(c)	three twelfths of the total amount of Legislation item 15 (Schedule B) of the said main estimates, $46,950;
(d)	two twelfths of the total amounts of External Affairs item 10, Secretary of State items 35, 40 and 45, Trade and Commerce item 29 (schedule C) of the said main estimates, $5,942,766.67;
(e)	one twelfth of the total amounts of Agriculture item 55, Finance item 10, National Film Board item 1 (Schedule D) of the said main estimates, $4,874,691.67;
(f)	seven twelfths of the total of all of the items set forth in the supplementary estimates A for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1968, laid before the House of Commons at the present session of parliament, $55,713,715.17;
(g)	four twelfths of the total amounts of loans, investments and advances items L40a and L112a (schedule E) of the said supplementary estimates, $4,416,666.67, be granted to Her Majesty on account of the fiscal year ending March 31, 1968.
